Build 026, from the 025 console runs:
- EDEN_NX2_UNIFIED_MEMORY (/data/eden-nx2/unified-memory.txt): images, device-local and upload buffers
  take the device-local host-visible memory types. VMA keeps 64 MiB blocks per memory type; at the 025
  crashes the device-local-only type held 460-970 MiB free inside its blocks while an upload buffer
  (another type) found the pool empty. Off by default; images and buffers fall back to their usual
  types when the shared ones do not suit them.
- Frame capture: /data/eden-nx2/capture-now.txt, created while the game runs, writes the 2D images
  drawn during the next frame to logs/capture/ (unswizzled, with an index), then deletes the file.
- EDEN_DEPTH_MODE: how many pipelines use -1..1 clip depth, and whether the driver converts it.
- The native shader key log names the program's slot (task/mesh/vertex/pixel/...), so reject-shaders.txt
  can skip one mesh program at a time.

